[{:db/id "q-93988/selection/be5beffd9a95134974e6bda496907ef99198947107984fe7477f4a7dcf5134a9" :answer/id #uuid "8718e058-9840-5ee6-a48a-8b27d7a19ec7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93988/selection/2e147b9bf74fe5a9fe1cc06d49c56b8c05578bddb93b65358c386cfaa2e4aa36" :answer/id #uuid "61e46203-1059-591e-95af-da38ec2ac388" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93988/selection/5f6c142a82c4a0bf971b412708f6830f8e50a71860d9c4cebbd361a473710cf0" :answer/id #uuid "c81a1868-219b-53c0-ac24-dcbfeee51e26" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93988/selection/f6ed8c3e8ac11c4c476e856e67261d9addd41c460d2f0404e6d3f3a72ad0633a" :answer/id #uuid "59937266-1e11-52f7-8c49-c94d9cc77827" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $Q$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93988/selection/3440ffb430bf09b9cc3be28b3ac0b5af1ddc80affb14810b6e5c974edac79ba7" :answer/id #uuid "4cde7000-5828-5298-b146-e89cb531eb2d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P,$ $Q,$ and $R$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-93988/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3440462d-31b6-59ed-925e-9362977e9e89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-93988/selection/2e147b9bf74fe5a9fe1cc06d49c56b8c05578bddb93b65358c386cfaa2e4aa36" :answer-field/choices ["q-93988/selection/be5beffd9a95134974e6bda496907ef99198947107984fe7477f4a7dcf5134a9" "q-93988/selection/2e147b9bf74fe5a9fe1cc06d49c56b8c05578bddb93b65358c386cfaa2e4aa36" "q-93988/selection/5f6c142a82c4a0bf971b412708f6830f8e50a71860d9c4cebbd361a473710cf0" "q-93988/selection/f6ed8c3e8ac11c4c476e856e67261d9addd41c460d2f0404e6d3f3a72ad0633a" "q-93988/selection/3440ffb430bf09b9cc3be28b3ac0b5af1ddc80affb14810b6e5c974edac79ba7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-93988" :question/id #uuid "25a8ea25-b1a6-5ebb-8991-b9d3238e32bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-93988" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are symmetric?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & \\sqrt{2} & 7 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}7 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $P$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $P={P}^{T}.$\n\n- $Q$ is *not* a symmetric matrix. Since ${q}_{12}\\ne {q}_{21},$ we obtain $Q\\ne {Q}^{T}.$\n\n$$\nQ=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- $R$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $R={R}^{T}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $R$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-93988/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c2da07e-23b5-58d0-aeef-14e21b329368"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-93988"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-96589/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "bca98281-a78b-5897-8882-67fd6710fbaa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96589/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "4a7ed82f-6ae1-59f8-930b-184b04edaadd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96589/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "635d63e7-7fa3-5f36-b58d-9c9d213bde26" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96589/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "10df0dd1-279a-5d23-a482-111282e7cd0a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96589/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "c918c971-61f4-58a4-9d51-26d10b88aacd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-96589/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "93da46da-c2e7-5e08-900a-46d5f09a262e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-96589/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-96589/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-96589/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-96589/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-96589/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-96589/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-96589" :question/id #uuid "c5ad1e1b-f3ae-5194-bf08-c8f143ac665d" :question/math-academy-id "q-96589" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $A$ is *any*  $n\\times n$ matrix, then ${A}^{2}$ is always symmetric.\n- The product of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric.\n- If $A$ is a symmetric matrix, then ${A}^{-1}$ is always symmetric (if it exists)." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. As a counterexample, consider the matrix \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nHowever, ${A}^{2}$ is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, consider the symmetric matrices \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nHowever, their product is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any non-singular symmetric matrix $A,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({A}^{-1})^{T} & =({A}^{T})^{-1} \\\\  & ={A}^{-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-96589/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bcd0ca26-3f22-533f-9d08-1533eeddbc79"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-96589"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143680/selection/5f6c142a82c4a0bf971b412708f6830f8e50a71860d9c4cebbd361a473710cf0" :answer/id #uuid "d27ab497-ceaf-5ef4-9a68-4412c3944c02" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143680/selection/2e147b9bf74fe5a9fe1cc06d49c56b8c05578bddb93b65358c386cfaa2e4aa36" :answer/id #uuid "59a76543-a774-5b9b-b5f0-1e17e9393afe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143680/selection/f6ed8c3e8ac11c4c476e856e67261d9addd41c460d2f0404e6d3f3a72ad0633a" :answer/id #uuid "7763240f-e922-5814-83ba-21a7c4162901" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$P$ and $Q$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143680/selection/afe4b97c823938f24ee0f462e6dae1ce1a6e74074abfb6f3f9af3b253499f0cc" :answer/id #uuid "87311d2b-b692-5387-8d7e-f90d38738534" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143680/selection/820282211c30a20e021a66f68b7464203ed7fe571ec86a81ae83e0d42d754f2c" :answer/id #uuid "b5cc5e49-d0e7-5fa2-9c23-7d0160ad40cd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$R$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143680/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a25362f-7a37-53ad-b176-ac4690cc5a2e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143680/selection/f6ed8c3e8ac11c4c476e856e67261d9addd41c460d2f0404e6d3f3a72ad0633a" :answer-field/choices ["q-143680/selection/5f6c142a82c4a0bf971b412708f6830f8e50a71860d9c4cebbd361a473710cf0" "q-143680/selection/2e147b9bf74fe5a9fe1cc06d49c56b8c05578bddb93b65358c386cfaa2e4aa36" "q-143680/selection/f6ed8c3e8ac11c4c476e856e67261d9addd41c460d2f0404e6d3f3a72ad0633a" "q-143680/selection/afe4b97c823938f24ee0f462e6dae1ce1a6e74074abfb6f3f9af3b253499f0cc" "q-143680/selection/820282211c30a20e021a66f68b7464203ed7fe571ec86a81ae83e0d42d754f2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143680" :question/id #uuid "75b778b3-42c6-58c1-87b6-db395f1a12f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-143680" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are symmetric?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 11 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -9 \\\\ 11 & -9 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $P$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $P={P}^{T}.$\n\n- $Q$ is a symmetric matrix. Indeed, $Q={Q}^{T}.$\n\n- $R$ is *not* a symmetric matrix. Since ${r}_{12}\\ne {r}_{21},$ we obtain $R\\ne {R}^{T}.$\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$P$ and $Q$ only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-143680/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c2da07e-23b5-58d0-aeef-14e21b329368"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143680"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143687/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "797ef5c8-6ccd-5ad9-bde4-d0940899a6a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143687/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "9ebc2625-8c3e-5089-ae2a-0b00470eb879" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143687/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "cd0f9501-1f4e-5760-8e72-616db8a35e1a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143687/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "9b4b2678-5772-554a-8a50-567b0d5d5599" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143687/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "c54b6bae-c139-5507-87e1-c3f8bc233780" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143687/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ff7e77df-ebf8-53c4-953e-4cbbdfd363b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143687/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-143687/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-143687/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-143687/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-143687/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-143687/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143687" :question/id #uuid "966e8499-782e-5d3b-b3cd-5b0bce9e8db5" :question/math-academy-id "q-143687" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The sum of two $n\\times n$ diagonal matrices is always symmetric.\n- If $A$ is *any*  $n\\times n$  matrix, then $A-{A}^{T}$ is always symmetric.\n- The product of two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any diagonal matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}+{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. As a counterexample, consider the matrix \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nHowever, $A-{A}^{T}$ is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-{A}^{T} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. As a counterexample, consider the symmetric matrices \n\n$\\,$ $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nHowever, their product is not symmetric:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-143687/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bcd0ca26-3f22-533f-9d08-1533eeddbc79"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143687"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-143688/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "3609c658-ab43-51fe-a392-9a9e2248b8a2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143688/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "f4a4c9f6-bc0c-542f-a9e7-88c82e1150db" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143688/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "d82885c3-b21a-5311-bda0-d1d153ffd013" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143688/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "36ce0de3-76df-5deb-ace6-2afd08e69c95" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143688/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "b2170d32-3899-5ed0-b686-f326535768a7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-143688/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1a0b28dc-2dd5-557a-9851-7bf252348c0e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-143688/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer-field/choices ["q-143688/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-143688/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-143688/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-143688/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-143688/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-143688" :question/id #uuid "0b4af280-6359-53fe-9a66-22b4e15e0bb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-143688" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- If $A$ is symmetric, then ${A}^{-1}$ is always symmetric (if it exists).\n- The sum of *any* two $n\\times n$ symmetric matrices is always symmetric.\n- If $A$ is *any*  $n\\times n$ matrix, then ${A}^{T}A$ is always symmetric." :question/worked-solution "A square matrix $A$ is symmetric if it is equal to its transpose:\n\n$$\nA={A}^{T}\n$$\n\nEquivalently, ${a}_{ij}={a}_{ji}$ for all $i,j.$ In other words, $A$ is symmetric across its main diagonal.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, for any non-singular symmetric matrix $A,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({A}^{-1})^{T} & =({A}^{T})^{-1} \\\\  & ={A}^{-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, for any two symmetric matrices $A$ and $B,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)^{T} & ={A}^{T}+{B}^{T} \\\\  & =A+B.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, for any $m\\times n$ matrix $A,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}({A}^{T}A)^{T} & ={A}^{T}({A}^{T})^{T} \\\\  & ={A}^{T}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-143688/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bcd0ca26-3f22-533f-9d08-1533eeddbc79"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-143688"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
